    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "an ablation study sounds like a lot of extra compute, and we're trying to keep the overhead low for this phase. \n\nhonestly, if the student model can't bridge that gap easily, the team might just decide to pivot. instead of pushing for a perfect distillation, they might just scale up a different, slightly larger student architecture that's more robust from the start. if that happens, we won't need to do the deeper troubleshooting on this current setup at all. \n\ndo you think there's a way to fix the reasoning plateau without making the process way more complex or expensive?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
